 4. Quoted: &quot;Cognitive atrophy&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 


 "When we challenged it hard, at least it was honest. It was like, 'Look, in the end, I'm better at sounding thorough than being thorough.'" — Goldman Sachs partner Chris Churchman in a new podcast on how the firm's AI platform admitted its own shortcomings, underscoring concerns that AI will lead to "cognitive atrophy" among the company's bankers. 
 
